/**
 * Planner application controller: owns the services (API, drafts, store), product data, local
 * previews and authoritative server results, and renders every component.
 *
 * Flow: GET /session → restore the autosaved workspace (or open #share / #add / #protocol) →
 * product details for every line → instant previews with engine.js → debounced (400 ms) POST
 * /calculate for the whole protocol; server results replace previews. Nothing typed by the user is
 * pre-filled, logged or put in a URL (only a new protocol's start date starts at today). Only
 * server-calculated quantities are ever added to the cart.
 *
 * Layout (CHANGE-1.1.0 §9, CHANGE-1.7.1 §2): toolbar, then — whenever the visitor can see a
 * pre-built protocol and no shared protocol is open — the entry choice "Pre-built protocols" /
 * "Make your own protocol", which shows one of two views: the pre-built protocols section, or the
 * two ARIA tabs — step 1 "Choose products" (popular combinations, all products, a summary bar with
 * "Plan quantities →") and step 2 "Plan & quantities" (protocol start date, product blocks,
 * timeline, "Your basket"). Without pre-built protocols there is no choice and the tabs are shown
 * as in 1.6.0. A compact bar fixed to the bottom of phone screens opens the basket.
 *
 * Pre-built protocols (internally "store protocols", CHANGE-1.7.0 §6.6–§6.11): amounts and times
 * per week are filled in only from a pre-built protocol the customer chose with "Use this protocol"
 * (replace or add, after the protocol's dialog has closed); every value stays editable. The lines
 * keep the tag "From a pre-built protocol" until the customer edits them (`storeOrigin`, kept in the
 * autosave meta only, never in the protocol document). Store managers can publish the workspace as
 * a pre-built protocol and open any of them from the admin (#store-protocol-edit=).
 *
 * Accessibility: removed lines leave an inline "Undo" placeholder (no time limit); focus is kept
 * clear of the fixed phone bar, toasts and theme toolbars (WCAG 2.4.11); unit changes convert or
 * clear the amount with an announced explanation (never relabel it).
 *
 * @module app
 */

